From: ENIAC Touch Kiosk <kiosk@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ft: default the repeat switches to 1 at startup

PROPOSED ONLY (spike #32). Not in patches/series: NFR-12 allows only the
mult.go patch until #36 decides otherwise.

f611c7f ("Rework function table code...") changed the repeat switch from
"rptsw = val - 1, compared with ring - 4" to "rptsw = val, compared with
the stage number (ring 1..9)". ftreset() now sets rptsw to 1, but nothing
sets it at startup, so a program whose rp switch is never set keeps
rptsw == 0. No stage matches 0, the ring counter climbs without bound
and the program never ends (sieve.e, lehmer.e). Before f611c7f the zero
value meant "repeat once", so those programs ran.

---
diff --git a/src/ft.go b/src/ft.go
--- a/src/ft.go
+++ b/src/ft.go
@@ -489,6 +489,12 @@
 
 	f := &ftable[unit]
 	f.ring = -3
+	// Repeat switches default to 1, as ftreset() sets them. Without this a
+	// program whose rp switch is never set (sieve.e, lehmer.e) has
+	// rptsw == 0, which no stage (1-9) matches, so the ring never resets.
+	for i := range f.rptsw {
+		f.rptsw[i] = 1
+	}
 	f.update = make(chan int)
 	go ftunit2(f)
 	f.resp = make(chan int)
